Recently the bike-share folks have been mapping out which docks to open and which dock every rider should be linked to. There’s a cost to open any dock and a separate inconvenience score for each rider depending on which opened dock they use, so the winning plan is simply the one with the smallest combined cost: the total of all dock-opening fees plus the total of all riders’ access costs. Nobody can be left without a registered dock or assigned to a dock that wasn’t opened, and docks don’t have limits on how many riders they can handle. The concrete details are shown below.

